						"@type": "Question",
						"name": "Can I use a self-hosted Proton Mail alternative with my own domain and any email client?",
						"acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes. Vectis Mail runs on your own VPS and speaks standard IMAP and SMTP, so any client — Thunderbird, Apple Mail, Outlook, mobile apps, mutt — connects directly with no bridge software. Custom domains are first-class: you point MX/DKIM/SPF/DMARC at your server and host unlimited addresses on it. Proton supports custom domains too, but only on paid plans, and third-party clients require running Proton Bridge locally to translate IMAP/SMTP into Proton's encrypted protocol. With Vectis there is no bridge and no per-plan domain cap — it is a normal mail server you own." }
