<body class="marketing-page">
	<SiteNav />

	<main>

	<section class="hero alt-hero">
		<div class="hero-badge">Alternatives · Private Email</div>
		<h1>Proton Mail alternative.<br/><span>Privacy you own, not rent.</span></h1>
		<p class="alt-lead">
			Proton Mail is privacy-as-a-service: hosted in Switzerland, encrypted so even
			Proton can't read your mail. Vectis Mail is privacy-as-ownership: a standard
			mail server you run on your own VPS, with your domain, standard IMAP/SMTP, and
			no third party in the loop at all. Different threat models — and we'll be
			straight about which one fits you, including where Proton is the better call.
		</p>
		<div class="alt-meta">
			<span>Last updated <time datetime={dateModified}>21 June 2026</time></span>
			<span>·</span>
			<img class="byline-avatar" src="/brand/imagery/ian-holt-avatar.webp" alt="" width="24" height="24" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /><span>Written by <a href="/about/" style="color:inherit;text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:2px">Ian Holt</a></span>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section" style="padding-top: 2rem;">
		<h2>The short answer</h2>
		<p class="subtitle">Two honest definitions of "private email" — pick the one that matches your risk.</p>
		<p>
			Choose <strong>Vectis Mail</strong> when you want to <em>own</em> your email
			infrastructure: your server, your keys, your domain, standard protocols, and no
			provider who could be breached, subpoenaed, price-changed, or shut down. Choose
			<strong>Proton Mail</strong> when you want <em>zero-ops, client-side encryption</em>
			where even the host can't read your message bodies, and you'd rather not run a server.
		</p>
		<p>
			The honest distinction up front: <strong>Vectis Mail is a standard mail server,
			not an end-to-end encrypted one.</strong> As the operator, you can read your own
			mail at rest — because you hold it, not a third party. Proton encrypts so that
			Proton can't. That's not Vectis falling short of Proton; it's a different goal.
			Proton protects you <em>from Proton</em>. Vectis removes the "from a provider"
			question entirely. Both are privacy. One you rent; one you own.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="section" style="padding-top: 1rem;">
